---
// src/pages/_site-updates/2026-10-26-homepage-headline-row.astro
export const updateMeta = {
  date: '2026-10-26',
  title: 'Homepage headline row and switching FAQs',
  tags: ['homepage', 'scout-ai', 'mobile', 'import', 'faq'],
};
---
<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">October 26, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    Added a row of three headline capabilities directly below the homepage hero: Scout AI, the Mobile App,
    and Bring What You Already Have. The hero itself is unchanged.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Pages updated</h3>
    <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li><a href="/" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">Homepage</a>: the headline row links to
        <a href="/workflows/scout-ai" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/workflows/scout-ai</a>,
        <a href="/mobile" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/mobile</a>, and
        <a href="/workflows/bring-what-you-have" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/workflows/bring-what-you-have</a>.</li>
      <li>The module grid gained a Go deeper line linking record import, applications and screening, and contracts and e-signatures.</li>
      <li>Three FAQ entries (switching without retyping, using your own contract, taking applications on your own website). They live in the page's <code>faqs</code> array, so the visible FAQ structured data carries them too.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Not yet linked</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      The payments and deposits page is not linked from the homepage until it is on the live site.
    </p>
  </div>
</article>
